54
00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:02.840
David: Now, if you change the behavior of the FAB format, you change the behavior of persistent hash.

55
00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:19.139
David: And there's backwards compatibility guaranteed for that, so it's probably not going to happen, which means that we should work towards stabilizing that format and work towards, bringing that format into, consistency with the existing spec.

